<%# System status: the setup wizard's own `Setup::SystemCheck` results,
    through the same rows, so both screens word every check identically.
    Here the rows sit in one card, divided inside it; the wizard keeps its
    ruled list (`setup/_system_check_results` takes the list's classes from
    its caller). A state is each row's chip and the summary line's words:
    there is no summary chip. "Run checks again" is a plain GET back to this
    screen, which re-runs every check -- idempotent, so a reload does the
    same. The time is the site's (`Admin::BaseController` runs every request
    in the site time zone). %>
<% content_for :title, t(".title") %>
<% passed = @results.count(&:ok?) %>
<div class="max-w-[900px]">
  <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink"><%= t(".title") %></h1>
      <p class="mt-1 text-small text-meta"><%= t(".summary", passed: passed, count: @results.size, time: I18n.l(Time.zone.now, format: :"admin.time")) %></p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to t(".run_again"), admin_system_status_path(**admin_url_options), class: Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.classes(:secondary),
          data: { turbo_prefetch: "false" } %>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-card bg-surface shadow-1">
    <%= render "setup/system_check_results", results: @results, copyable: true, list_class: "divide-y divide-line px-4",
          mail_settings_href: (admin_settings_path(anchor: "mail", **admin_url_options) if can?("settings.manage")),
          image_settings_href: (admin_settings_path(anchor: "images", **admin_url_options) if can?("settings.manage")),
          forms_href: (admin_forms_path(**admin_url_options) if %w[forms.manage form_submissions.view].any? { |key| can?(key) }) %>
  </div>
</div>
